From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: Keep live sources in the loading network
 state.

The engine switches to MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_NETWORK_IDLE as soon as the source
is opened. That suits a file, but a live source (no MF_PD_DURATION, so an
infinite duration) keeps fetching data for as long as it plays, which is
MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_NETWORK_LOADING in the HTML5 networkState model the media
engine follows.

AVPro Video (VRChat's TopazPlayer) treats a live stream reporting IDLE as
stalled and reloads it repeatedly, so live RTSP/RTMP streams never settle.
Leave live sources in the loading state; files keep the current behavior.

Analysis and initial patch by l12436 (GitHub).

Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/892

Not runtime-tested: needs a TopazPlayer live stream in VRChat.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -1728,7 +1728,9 @@
 
     if (SUCCEEDED(hr))
     {
-        engine->network_state = MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_NETWORK_IDLE;
+        /* A live source keeps fetching data for as long as it plays. */
+        engine->network_state = isinf(engine->duration) ? MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_NETWORK_LOADING
+                : MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_NETWORK_IDLE;
         if (start_playback)
             media_engine_start_playback(engine);
         else
